Scope

The licence above covers the source code of Fable 2: Return to Albion itself.
It does not cover:

- Third-party code. Everything under a `thirdparty/` directory, and every git
  submodule (rexglue-sdk, Fable2AssetBrowser, ncnn, zlib), keeps the licence
  found beside it. That includes FFmpeg and libmspack, which are LGPL-2.1 or
  later.

- Code derived from rexglue-sdk, including `rexglue-net/shadow/`. It is
  available under the BSD 3-Clause licence in `rexglue-net/rexglue-sdk/LICENSE`:

      Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay
      Portions derived from the Xenia project:
      Copyright (c) 2022, Ben Vanik and Xenia project contributors

- Fable 2 itself. This project ships no game code or data. The recompiled game
  code that a build generates, and every game asset, belong to their owners.
  You need your own copy of the game.

Contributions made before this file changed to MIT were made under the BSD
3-Clause licence, Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay, whose conditions still apply to
those contributions.
